WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.900
The read side has two parts.

2
00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:05.512
VK-INT-07 is the gate.

3
00:00:05.512 --> 00:00:09.230
The validation kit's check
reads the migration reports,

4
00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:14.643
and fails on any GPO targeted in Active
Directory whose readiness isn't complete,

5
00:00:14.643 --> 00:00:17.713
and on any in-scope GPO
that was never imported.

6
00:00:17.713 --> 00:00:21.150
It works per GPO, and
doesn't read the settings.

7
00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:23.025
The move plan works per setting.

8
00:00:23.025 --> 00:00:25.588
It reads each report's setting mappings,

9
00:00:25.588 --> 00:00:30.713
which Learn's Graph beta reference documents,
and gives every row a disposition.

10
00:00:30.713 --> 00:00:33.012
The dispositions are the kit's design.

11
00:00:33.012 --> 00:00:36.725
A candidate is supported and has
an Intune setting definition,

12
00:00:36.725 --> 00:00:38.938
and a person decides whether it moves.

13
00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:43.375
A conflict is two GPOs setting one
definition to different values:

14
00:00:43.375 --> 00:00:46.763
Learn's page on creating
a settings catalog policy

15
00:00:46.763 --> 00:00:50.151
from imported GPOs says
Migrate stops on that case.

16
00:00:50.151 --> 00:00:52.487
The decision record picks the value.

17
00:00:52.487 --> 00:00:57.200
AppLocker and firewall settings go to
Endpoint security, as that page says.

18
00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:01.629
And, in this workbook's guidance, the
plan decides nothing: Group Policy

19
00:01:01.629 --> 00:01:06.340
analytics finds the landing zone, never
whether a setting is still needed.
